# Semgrep ignore list (issue #33). Each entry has a justification and is listed in
# docs/report/deviations.md. Anything not listed here is scanned.

# Tests: they contain fixed dummy values (TOTP secrets, one-time codes, passwords) that the
# generic-secret rule flags, and test-only constructs (default arguments with dummy passwords,
# `len(list)` in assertions, local URL checks) that the Python packs flag. None of them is a real
# credential or runs in production, and test files are not part of any image (the Dockerfiles
# copy only the sources). A custom .semgrepignore replaces Semgrep's built-in default list,
# so tests/ has to be named here.
**/*.test.ts
**/*.test.tsx
backend/tests/

# Development mock of the API: only loaded by the Vite dev server (vite.config.ts), never built
# into the image. Its demo TOTP secret is a fixed dummy value.
frontend/dev-mock-api.ts
